  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f867e729cd163844296773769e23f97f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Oswen
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Rarety: 2
  m_Description: "Born of scale and wisdom, Oswen was once a daughter of the Aztkal\u2019s
    southern reaches \u2014 a quiet scholar from a humble village hidden among emerald
    marshes. That peace was shattered when the Savage Horde came howling from the
    wastes.\n\nThey descended upon her homeland like beasts unleashed from the abyss.
    The orcish marauders did not merely kill \u2014 they ravaged. They burned homes
    for amusement, tore limbs from captives to test their strength, and left the
    corpses to rot beneath the open sky. When the Horde moved on, only ruin and screams
    remained \u2014 and amid that ruin, one survivor : Oswen\n\nGrief hardened into
    vengeance, and vengeance into purpose. For years, she hunted the Horde across
    desolate plains and blood-soaked roads, striking from shadows yet never finding
    the victory she sought, despite her many tries.\n\nSo she turned to another weapon
    : the forbidden veins of sorcery \u2014 the dark magic of corruption and decay.
    In tombs forgotten by even the dead, she mastered the art of blight: crafting
    diseases that ate flesh from bone, curses that withered crops, and vapors that
    turned air to poison. Her own blood grew tainted with this craft, her scales
    darkening to the hue of old iron, her eyes gleaming with the fever of forbidden
    knowledge.\n\nThrough cunning and patience, Oswen rose among her kin. Her sharp
    mind earned her a place in the royal court, where wisdom and deceit walk hand
    in hand. \nAs High Magus and advisor, she wielded influence like a blade \u2014
    sharp, silent, and deadly. Behind the polished marble of the palace, she continued
    her secret work: experiments on those who would not be missed, victims of ambition
    and opportunity alike.\n\nShe seeks no redemption. Only vengeance.\nEach life
    taken, each body consumed by rot, feeds her growing power \u2014 a power born
    from pain, honed by hate."
  m_SpellElements: 04000000
